      ":question/problem": "An aquarium builder restricts tank dimensions for a standard shelf. For tanks shaped like rectangular prisms, the sum of the perimeter of the base and the height must not exceed $160$ inches. The perimeter of the base is calculated using the width and length. If a tank has a height of $40$ inches and its length is $1.5$ times its width, which inequality represents the possible values of the width $w$, in inches?"
